  "notes": "USAGE:\nCarries a literary, romantic quality when describing travel with no fixed plans. In negative contexts, can imply vagrancy or aimlessness. Often used with の to modify nouns: {放浪|ほうろう}の{旅|たび} (wandering journey), {放浪|ほうろう}の{画家|がか} (wandering painter).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {放浪|ほうろう}の{旅|たび}: a wandering journey\n- {各地|かくち}を{放浪|ほうろう}する: to wander from place to place\n- {放浪|ほうろう}{生活|せいかつ}: a nomadic life\n- {放浪|ほうろう}{者|しゃ}: a wanderer, vagrant",
